Instagram Module — End‑to‑End System Design (Safety‑First)
1. Objective & Boundary

The Instagram module enables user‑authorized account management for messaging‑based outreach while prioritizing account longevity over throughput. The system is designed to reduce abnormal patterns, avoid correlated failures, and fail safely under uncertainty. All actions occur only on accounts explicitly connected by the user.

2. Core Principles (Non‑Negotiable)

Continuity over simulation: Automation must look like a continuation of existing behavior, never a behavioral reset.

Isolation by default: Every IG account operates inside its own execution capsule (identity, schedule, state).

Risk‑weighted execution: Accounts with weaker signals automatically receive reduced capability.

Stop > Recover: Any ambiguity or friction results in pause, not compensation.

Determinism beats cleverness: Rules override AI; AI never drives execution.

3. System Components
3.1 Account Capsule

Each connected Instagram account is represented as a sealed unit:

Persistent session state

Stable device context

Historical behavior profile

Risk score (rolling, decaying)

No shared state exists between capsules.

3.2 Campaign Engine (IG‑Specific)

Campaigns are intent pipelines, not action queues.

Each campaign defines:

Entry method (DM only / Story‑based / Highlight‑based)

Message phases (initial + follow‑ups)

Eligibility rules (based on recon & prior interaction)

Exit conditions (reply, friction, silence threshold)

Execution is event‑driven, not volume‑driven.

3.3 Message Strategy Layer

First contact is context‑light and non‑transactional

No outbound escalation without inbound signals

Follow‑ups degrade in assertiveness, never escalate

Templates are treated as semantic blueprints, not text blocks

AI is used only for variation + tone matching, never for deciding when or how much.

4. Execution Model (How Actions Happen)
4.1 Temporal Control

Activity windows are probabilistic, not scheduled

Start/stop times drift over long horizons

Inactive days are expected and enforced

4.2 Action Selection

At any execution opportunity, the system chooses:

Act (message / view)

Observe (scroll / view only)

Exit (do nothing)

Non‑action is a first‑class outcome.

4.3 Entry Method Logic

Direct DM: Used only when profile signals indicate prior openness

Story / Highlight path: Treated as context gathering, not engagement farming

System never chains multiple entry methods tightly

5. Volume & Pace Governance

No fixed quotas exposed internally

All limits are relative to account age, stability, and recent friction

System reduces output automatically under:

Message failures

UI inconsistencies

Latency anomalies

Users request intent, system decides capacity.

6. Content Safety & Pattern Control

Language avoids transactional framing in early stages

Structural diversity enforced across messages

No deterministic phrasing, punctuation, or CTA patterns

No forced “human errors” or stylized quirks

Natural variance emerges from context, not randomness.

7. Follow‑Up Governance

Follow‑ups require:

Time separation

Tone shift

Justification (new context or value)

Silence is treated as a signal, not a failure

Replies immediately lock the thread and halt automation

8. Detection & Self‑Protection Layer
8.1 Early Friction Signals

UI challenges

Message send inconsistencies

Session interruptions

Unexpected reauthentication

Any single signal triggers immediate suspension.

8.2 Cooldown & Recovery

Cooldowns are longer than the triggering anomaly

Resume state is degraded, not restored

Repeated friction permanently lowers capability

There is no “push through” mode.

9. AI Agent Role (Strictly Bounded)

AI may:

Rephrase text

Infer tone

Generate semantic variants

AI may NOT:

Control timing

Decide volume

Trigger actions

Override safety states

10. Failure Containment

One account failure never affects others

No shared execution threads

No shared timing patterns

No synchronized campaigns

Blast radius is intentionally one account wide.

11. What This System Explicitly Avoids

Behavioral imitation scripts

Fixed numeric thresholds

Forced engagement

Multi‑platform coupling

Aggressive recovery logic